A share whose last ready thread waits stays on the queue it waited on.
Its next turn would find no thread to run;
the queues hold only shares with a ready thread.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a queue holds a share it is not for

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -147,7 +147,7 @@ static struct share **share_queue(const struct share *s)
 static void share_settle(struct share *s)
 {
     struct share **queue = share_queue(s);
-    if (queue != s->queue) {
+    if (queue != NULL && queue != s->queue) {
         if (s->queue != NULL) {
             share_remove(s);
         }
